  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Turn across, drop and through ball",
  "description": "Two groups, A and B, plus a goalkeeper in each goal. A and B start on the same wing in their own half, B deeper towards their own goal.\n\nThe goalkeeper throws out to A, who skates towards the ball. A turns in and skates across the rink. B sets off at the same time and must be at high speed. A drops the ball back towards their own goal to B and turns upfield. Both head for the far goal; B plays a through ball to A, who finishes. Rotation: A goes to B and B to A.\n\nProgression: a third player skates across, takes the throw-out and passes to A. Switch sides after a while. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "B must be at full speed before the drop pass – A must be at full speed after it."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Drop the ball back so B can take it forward without slowing down."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "B may need to hold back slightly after receiving so A gets ahead before the final pass."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Play the through ball in front of A, into the space they are skating into."
    }
  ],
